```java
class Pizza {
    String size;
    boolean cheese;

    // BAD: validation/defaults duplicated in every constructor
    Pizza() {
        this.size = "medium";
        this.cheese = false;                     // duplicated
    }
    Pizza(String size) {
        this.size = size;
        this.cheese = false;                     // duplicated again
    }
    Pizza(String size, boolean cheese) {
        this.size = size;
        this.cheese = cheese;
    }
    // If you add validation, you must add it to ALL THREE constructors.
}
```

```java
class Pizza {
    String size;
    boolean cheese;

    Pizza() {
        this("medium");              // delegates to Pizza(String)
    }
    Pizza(String size) {
        this(size, false);           // delegates to the primary constructor
    }
    Pizza(String size, boolean cheese) {         // PRIMARY CONSTRUCTOR
        if (size == null) throw new IllegalArgumentException("size required");
        this.size = size;
        this.cheese = cheese;       // validation and assignment in ONE place
    }
}

Pizza p1 = new Pizza();                    // -> medium, no cheese
Pizza p2 = new Pizza("large");             // -> large, no cheese
Pizza p3 = new Pizza("large", true);       // -> large, with cheese
```

*`this(...)` must be the **first statement** — any code before it is a compile error.*

```java
class Rectangle {
    int width;
    int height;

    Rectangle() {                               // convenience: 1x1 default
        this(1, 1);                             // MUST be the first statement
    }

    Rectangle(int side) {                       // convenience: square
        this(side, side);                       // delegates to primary
    }

    Rectangle(int width, int height) {          // PRIMARY CONSTRUCTOR
        if (width <= 0 || height <= 0)
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("dimensions must be positive");
        this.width = width;                     // field assignment in ONE place
        this.height = height;
    }
}

Rectangle r1 = new Rectangle();     // width=1, height=1
Rectangle r2 = new Rectangle(5);    // width=5, height=5 (square)
Rectangle r3 = new Rectangle(4, 6); // width=4, height=6
```

